TIL Parse Method Analysis Plan

Scope window: 06/08 to 06/12
Primary comparison: DS foundation parsing vs Databricks ai_parse_document

1. Objective
Evaluate parsing quality and runtime readiness using deterministic, reviewer-auditable metrics.

2. Test set for gating
Use 5-doc gate set to avoid overfitting to one file.
1. 1603-R2
2. 2284
3. 1502-2R1
4. 1937-R2
5. 1945-R2

Use the 25-doc pilot as secondary evidence after gate set evaluation.

3. Core experiments
1. Side-by-side parser diff
Run both parsers on the same PDF and compare section-level output.
Measure: section coverage, read-order breaks, table loss, noise ratio.

2. Double-column reading order check
Review dense-layout pages for column interleaving errors.
Measure: sentence continuity error rate per page.

3. Formula and fraction fidelity check
Validate Combined Wet Time expression and key numeric thresholds.
Measure: exact formula match and numeric preservation.

4. Table capture fidelity check
Validate compliance table, timing table, and wet inlet interval table.
Measure: row completeness, column alignment, heading preservation, unit-value correctness.

5. Boilerplate suppression experiment
Compare raw vs cleaned outputs.
Measure: token reduction and false-removal rate of meaningful content.

6. Structured field stability test
Repeat profile extraction 3 runs from same extracted text.
Measure: variance of critical fields across runs.

7. Evidence traceability check
Verify source snippets for key profile fields.
Measure: field-to-evidence coverage and evidence mismatch rate.

8. Image-text usefulness check
Evaluate whether image descriptions add signal or noise.
Measure: useful image entries ratio and downstream impact.

9. Markdown-first reviewability check
Perform SME-style review on markdown artifacts.
Measure: review time, clarity score, and missing-context count.

10. JSON contract validation
Validate extracted_document and profile_response against agreed schema.
Measure: required-field pass rate, null handling, list-shape consistency.

11. Confidence calibration check
Compare model confidence against deterministic quality score.
Measure: rank-order alignment only, not absolute trust.

4. Deterministic scoring model
Compute per-document quality score from deterministic metrics.

Weights:
1. Extraction completeness: 25%
2. Structural fidelity: 25%
3. Traceability: 20%
4. Noise control: 15%
5. Consistency: 15%

Metric definitions:
1. Extraction completeness
Required sections found: purpose, compliance, timing, recommendations, references, thresholds.

2. Structural fidelity
Formula integrity, table preservation, and read-order correctness.

3. Traceability
Critical profile fields mapped to valid source snippets.

4. Noise control
Boilerplate plus OCR/vision gibberish ratio in final review artifact.

5. Consistency
Critical field stability across repeated runs.

5. Quantitative acceptance gates
Per-document gates:
1. Extraction completeness >= 0.90
2. Structural fidelity >= 0.90
3. Traceability >= 0.90
4. Noise score >= 0.75
5. Consistency >= 0.95
6. Formula fidelity for critical formulas = 1.00

Gate-set decision (5 docs):
1. At least 4 of 5 docs must pass all per-document gates
2. No doc may fail formula fidelity
3. Mean final quality score across gate set >= 0.88

6. Confidence score policy
Model confidence is non-gating and auxiliary.
Use it only for calibration analysis against deterministic score.
Do not use model confidence alone to approve parser readiness.

7. Reproducibility controls
Capture per run:
1. Parser name and version
2. Model name and version
3. Prompt or template hash
4. Input PDF checksum
5. Run timestamp and run id

8. Outputs to produce for review
1. Per-doc comparison sheet (DS vs Databricks)
2. Deterministic scorecard with pass/fail by metric
3. Confidence calibration summary
4. Recommendation note: parser choice and runtime hardening actions